{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he shall take for the one being purified.</b> The priest takes from his own. <b>For the one being purified</b> — whether man or woman, whether minor boy or minor girl. From here they said: items acquired for a man are valid for a woman; for a woman, valid for a man; for a metzora, valid for a house." "<b>Two birds.</b> Wherever צפור is stated, the verse speaks of a clean species. R. Yitzchak said: a clean bird is called עוף and is called צפור, but an unclean bird is called only עוף." "<b>Clean ones.</b> And not unclean ones, and not טרפות." "<b>And cedar wood.</b> R. Chanina ben Gamliel says: ובראשו טרף."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:08.402636199Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}